# Mirrors `lighter_adaptive_ensemble_bots/.gitignore` deliberately: the two
# packages have the same shape, so the same policy belongs in the same place
# rather than as a second copy in the ROOT .gitignore. A root rule would also
# be anchored there and would sit far from the code that writes these files.

# Generated reports. Every one is reproducible from a command in the README
# (`backtest`, `walk-forward`, `sensitivity`), and the only data this package
# ships is SYNTHETIC, written by `make-examples` from a seed -- so a committed
# copy buys nothing and goes stale. `.gitkeep` is NOT matched: the directory
# itself stays tracked so a fresh clone has somewhere to write.
reports/*.json
reports/*.txt
reports/*.log

# Synthetic example tapes -- regenerate with `make-examples --seed N`, which is
# byte-identical for the same seed.
data/examples/*.json

# Runtime state is per-machine and per-run.
state/*.json
state/*.tmp
state/*.db

# The kill switch is an operational act, never a committed file.
runtime/KILL_SWITCH

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
